    "turn_text": "you know, to be frank, I was given recent rulings. I was managing my expectations for what today's ruling could be. That being said, it's important that your listeners know that Mr. Presone is safe. It is effective. It is illegal. more than in cases where Mr. Stone is used to manage miscarriage or abortion care more than half of people in need of support around miscarriage management or abortion care used with a pre-stone. It is safer than Tylenol. And again, it is safe, effective, and legal. So today's ruling, it is a relief. It's a victory for anyone who has or will ever need this essential medical or medication abortion care. And I also want to say that it doesn't mean that in any way we are waning, you know, in our efforts because this case was really just a continuation of DOG. You know, the dominoes have continued to fall after DOG. They started with abortion access and they moved to birth control, contraceptive, yes. So this was just one more step in that broader march towards a nationwide ban on abortion. So I'm feeling relieved today is certainly a victory, but I certainly am not under the impression that anti-abortion extremists are not going to continue their coordinated efforts at every level of government to continue to try to rip away this critical health care for millions of people.",
