    "turn_text": "You know, Congresswoman, you are urging people and it's very close. Only a few seats need to switch hands and if the, in the House and if the Democrats maintain their, both their quote, majority because of the vice president, that assumes that Joe Biden is reelected. Obviously things could change in Congress. But at the same time, we, one of the things, Margaret and I've been preaching for years, that seems to fall on relatively deaf ears is how important the presidential decision is For one particular reason is that person chooses justices to the Supreme Court. The two oldest justices are the two most conservative, Alito and Thomas. I love the belief that if Trump is reelected, they both resign at some point during his four years and he picks 40-year-old versions of Trump and Alito who serve for 40 more years. Do you agree that people don't make the connection as clearly as they could between that incredibly important decision that presidents make and how it affects their lives?",
