    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/1/91703.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 13,
    "turn_text": "I agree. People don't make that connection and we also have a messengers that seek to, you know, revise and rewrite history. And you see that with Donald Trump every day, who's trying to backwalk the role that he played in the Dobbs decision. So Supreme Court justices, I mean, as we have seen in recent years, they've been enlisted as co-conspirators and accomplices in actually the absence of justice and working actively to overturn the will of the majority of the people. And that is true for Dobbs, that is true on affirmative action and a host of other issues. So as I said, going into this, for today's ruling, I had managed my expectation. But I am relieved this is a critical victory. And again, they had no legal standing. And if a person is safe, effective, and it is legal. And it is essential medical care in miscarriage management or abortion care.",
