    "turn_text": "Well, yes, I do think that we should continue to call the question, you know, a firm to every elected official. If this is an issue of priority for you, that this matters, that it is not hyperbole to say it's a matter of life and death. You know, again, a nationwide ban on abortion is a nation of forced birth, and so it has severe consequences and ramifications. When it comes to reproductive rights, when it comes to maternal justice, when it comes to a growing maternal morbidity crisis amongst Black women disproportionately when it comes to abortion, justice and access. And again, fundamentally, it's a matter of bodily autonomy and freedom and health care, which is a human right. And Jim, to your earlier point about the court, which this is a conversation for another day, but certainly I am of the belief that we need to. You know, we need a call of ethics, a standard. We need reforms. We need to expand the court. And there is growing momentum around that, certainly given recent actions by justices which put their integrity and ethics into great questions. But on the issue of the courts and on the issue of abortion access, Please look no further than Project 2025. This",
